// CROWN modal (§11 6.3's opening walk, measured 2026-08-08; the
// mechanism narration corrected same day, and the PREMISE corrected
// 2026-09-27): a closure performing E, born UNDER an install, escaping
// it — the latent/performed distinction. E rides the closure's VALUE row;
// `escaped`'s own row stays pure, so no negation anywhere refuses the
// birth (expect NO E_EffectMismatch). What the escaped closure needs is a
// live install AT THE CALL: this file used to call it bare at main and
// claimed the "static singleton tier" served it — the tiers are deleted,
// every perform walks the live chain, and the bare call ABORTED at
// runtime (exit 134) while the compile gate cleared E because h was
// installed somewhere. The root gate reads the row alone now, so the bare
// call is leak-root-escape's refusal; here the call runs under h and the
// program runs to 1.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(1) }
fn make() = () => op()
fn escaped() = (make()) ~> h
fn main() = (escaped()()) ~> h
